@@ -0,0 +1,752 @@
+From: Andy <andylee77@users.noreply.github.com>
+Subject: [PATCH] infinity6c: GC8613 sensor driver
+
+Adds sensor_gc8613_mipi.c, a from-source driver for the GalaxyCore GC8613
+(3840x2160 10-bit, 4-lane MIPI), with its init table, gain curve and timing
+reversed from the vendor module. Load with chmap=1 lane_num=4.
+
+It builds against the sensor-src headers that match 1230's mi.ko (the set
+before fe5d953), which sigmastar-sensor-headers supplies.
+
+---
+diff --git a/infinity6c/sensor-src/sensor_gc8613_mipi.c b/infinity6c/sensor-src/sensor_gc8613_mipi.c
+new file mode 100644
+index 0000000..72a968e
+--- /dev/null
++++ b/infinity6c/sensor-src/sensor_gc8613_mipi.c
+@@ -0,0 +1,735 @@
++/*
++ * sensor_gc8613_mipi.c - GalaxyCore GC8613 (8MP, MIPI 4-lane, 10-bit) driver
++ * for SigmaStar Infinity6C (SSC378DE) under the ms_cus_sensor framework.
++ *
++ * Written from source against johnchia's sensor-src/include/drv_ms_cus_sensor.h
++ * so the ms_cus_sensor ABI/offsets match the 1230 mi.ko by construction
++ * (the OEM prebuilt .ko ABI-crashes mi.ko). Register tables, gain curve, mode
++ * timing and power sequence were reverse-engineered from the unit's own OEM
++ * driver gc8613YA_MIPI_10bit_v2.2_20241015.ko (build 202410151157). Template:
++ * sensor_gc4653_mipi.c (same GalaxyCore register conventions).
++ *
++ * Target: Anpviz IPC-D3B83B-S / UVision MC-A85. Load: chmap=1 lane_num=4.
++ * ISP IQ reuses the IMX307 profile (OEM iqfile0-3 -> imx307_iqfile.bin).
++ * GPL-2.0.
++ */
++
